    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nWhen acd it turned off (`:set noacd`), the explorer (`:lua MiniFiles.open()`) is open in cwd (`:lua print(vim.fn.getcwd())`).\r\nIt would be nice to have an option to navigate to the folder of the last buffer.\r\n\r\nScenario:\r\n1. `:set noacd`\r\n2. navigate to a file in a different folder\r\n3. `:lua MiniFiles.open()`\r\n4. press backspace to reset, the explorer will point at the original cwd\r\n5. press q to close the explorer\r\n6. `:lua MiniFiles.open()`\r\n7. the explorer will open in the original cwd, not in the folder of the current buffer\r\n\r\nThe desired behaviour is:\r\n7. the explorer opens in the folder of current buffer\r\nor\r\n7. press some key, similarly to `<BS>` to navigate to the folder of the current buffer\r\n",
