            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThis is already possible through the [`path`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/74e6b722c91113bc70d4bf67249ed8de0642b20e/doc/mini-files.txt#L655) argument of `open()`. In particular, [supplying path to current buffer](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/74e6b722c91113bc70d4bf67249ed8de0642b20e/doc/mini-files.txt#L644-L645) will open directory of current file focused on the file. This can be made more streamlined with a custom mapping.\r\n\r\nClosing as already possible.",
